ally  good for me as someone who's experienced  constantly turning on their old switch  from standby mode and it's saying  battery dead or whatever it was like you  have to recharge it so all things  considered it's really good the the  rated battery life is less than that of  the improved standard switch model but  you know I'll be honest like I was I was  pretty impressed with what they were  able to get out of this device because  it is smaller which means the battery  itself has to be smaller  okay there are a lot of folks who  primarily play their switch on the go  and held only there's a lot of  conversations about you know should I  got a switch light or not is this for me  and I imagine that that crowd is  probably looking at this thing a lot  harder than maybe other people who  already have a normal switch and docket  occasionally yeah what would you say to  them about the switch light is this up  their alley consider what games you want  to play if you only want to be a single  player gamer at least in terms of like  local you know situations then yeah  maybe this is fine right maybe you'll  play with your friends online but if you  want to get together and play with other  people who maybe don't have joy cons or  pro controllers and you need to supply  them you need to seriously consider why  you're choosing this because if you need  to go that route  and pick up new controllers you're  coming so close to the cost of the full  price switch right which has built-in  controllers has all the features that  this doesn't this also doesn't have like  Rumble at all let alone just HD Rumble  it has none so you know that's sort of  like a secondary thing but really it  comes down to is this a personal device  or is this a device you want to share  with other people that's the biggest  question you need to ask the alternative  is that this could be your second switch  or really your primary switch Nintendo  does allow you to share accounts across  devices your primary device doesn't have  to be online if you want to use that  profile on any secondary devices have to  be online if you want them to access  your library of games and saves it so  you could in theory buy this and get  your primary switch leave your standard  switch at home as your secondary one  because it's probably always connected  to Wi-Fi and you can have two switches  one of them being a very portable  version it also feels really good to  play well there you have it that's  Peters review of the switch light you  can check out the full written review on  gamespot comm you could also check out a  fact that we have to answer all your  questions about the switch light and we  also have a guide to transfer your  accounts between your switch and a  switch light if that's what's gonna get  it to so thank you for watching and take  the game spot for all our coverage  [Music]

